:499`) and the goldens fixture (lines 64/82/167). No artifact store records turned up, most likely because the search skipped the `.insrc/` directory (hidden or gitignored). So the evidence cannot confirm or refute any of the counts: 731 records, 80 BUILD / 29 approved with failed tasks, 148 CR / 73 orphaned, 39 LLDs with no PLAN, 141/141 LLDs missing sizeClass, 7+1 missing route stamps, 326 reviewed artifacts with no meta.updatedAt. The absence of `sizeClass`/`updatedAt` matches is consistent with the \"none\" claims, but only because the store was never searched. That is not evidence for them. The premise is UNVERIFIABLE.","action":"Re-run the probe against the store itself (for example `rg --hidden --no-ignore` or a jq/node count script over `.insrc/artifacts/*.json`) and record the resulting counts in the artifact as a reproducible command plus its output. If the counts are only there to size the backfill and every record will be processed anyway, rewrite them as approximate or snapshot-dated.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence never touched .insrc/artifacts, so no count can be corrected from it. Any edit would invent values. The premise needs re-grounding, not a mechanical text fix.","options":["Re-run the inventory with a hidden/no-ignore search (or a jq/node script) over .insrc/artifacts/*.json and update each count to match the output.","Keep the counts but label them as a dated snapshot (2026-10-07), and add the exact command that reproduces them so a reviewer can re-check.","If the work processes every matching record whatever the totals, drop the exact numbers and state the selection criteria instead (BUILD approved with failed tasks, CR without a BUILD, LLD without a PLAN, etc.)."]}},{"claimId":"p27","ref":"c1","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"docs/insrc-delivery-board-prd.html:193 (FR-09) requires a read-only MVP leaving artifacts, approvals, code and Git state unchanged; §05 at :164 and §07 at :197.","evidence":"The read of docs/insrc-delivery-board-prd.html:193 returned `<tr><td>FR-09</td><td>Keep the MVP read-only: all navigation and filtering leave artifacts, approvals, code, and Git state unchanged.</td><td>Must</td></tr>`. That matches the premise word for word: FR-09 is a Must requirement for a read-only MVP that leaves artifacts, approvals, code and Git state unchanged. The grep for /Keep the MVP read-only/ found the same text in DEF.md:200 (citation c1), which quotes the PRD accurately. No evidence was gathered for the secondary anchors :164 (§05 State & evidence) and :197 (§07 Data contract), so those section-location pointers are not verified. The premise's requirement rests on FR-09 at :193, though, and that line is confirmed.","action":"None needed; the FR-09 claim is verified. Optionally, re-check that :164 and :197 still point to the §05 and §07 headings if the citation will be used for navigation. That does not change what gets built.","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The primary anchor (:193, FR-09) is confirmed word for word. The §05/§07 anchors at :164 and :197 are unprobed supporting pointers, and the read-only requirement does not depend on them, so no edit is warranted."}},{"claimId":"p28","ref":"c2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"docs/plans/delivery-board-epics.md:54-55 defines E1 as a read-only daemon-owned projection of .insrc/artifacts/ into the PRD's work-item model, exposed over IPC.","evidence":"The premise checks out against the source. A read of docs/plans/delivery-board-epics.md:54 returns \"**Goal:** one read-only, daemon-owned projection that turns\". The grep for /daemon-owned projection/ finds that same line. It also finds the DEF.md:201 citation [[c2]], which attributes the full quote to delivery-board-epics.md:54-55 under the heading \"(E1 — Delivery read model (daemon))\": \"one read-only, daemon-owned projection that turns `.insrc/artifacts/` into the PRD's work-item model, exposed over IPC.\" The read only covered line 54. The rest of the sentence (\"into the PRD's work-item model, exposed over IPC\") is on line 55. It comes from the artifact's own quote, but that quote fits seamlessly onto the line-54 fragment that was read. The anchor resolves to E1's goal statement, so the premise holds.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The anchor resolves to E1's goal line and its text matches the premise. No edit is needed."}},{"claimId":"p29","ref":"c22","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"docs/plans/vscode-viewer-gaps.md:86-90 (Track B1) leaves open which surface owns which anchor kind.","evidence":"The cited anchor checks out. Reading docs/plans/vscode-viewer-gaps.md:86 returns \"Design question for this track: `workflow.resolveComment` anchors to document…\", which opens Track B1's design question. A grep then matches docs/plans/vscode-viewer-gaps.md:89: \"…The design has to state which surface owns which anchor kind rather [than growing both]\". The doc treats surface-to-anchor-kind ownership as a decision still to be made, which means it is still open. That matches the premise. The DEF's citation [[c22]] at DEF.md:220 quotes the same sentence and gives the same range (86-90). The DEF uses this point only to explain why review annotations are deferred as a follow-on capability (DEF.md:75). That use is consistent with the source.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"Verified: the cited lines frame anchor ownership as an open design question, as the premise says. No edit needed."}},{"claimId":"p30","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"s2, s3 and s4 depend on s1; s5 depends on s1, s2, s3 and s4.","evidence":"No probes were run for this premise, so there are no ripgrep matches or path:line reads. Nothing in the evidence confirms or contradicts the dependency ordering (s2, s3 and s4 depend on s1; s5 depends on s1 through s4). The premise i